{
  "description": "Full vibrational Raman of LiH (HF, one rung: protocol 1e-4, k 6, l 50): alpha(0) xyz, the complete static polarizability gradient over all 3N = 6 nuclear coordinates (raman.nuc_atom -1; 54 rows under response_properties.raman), the Hessian assembled from the same six nuclear response states (vibrational_analysis), and the one vibrational mode with its Raman activity and depolarization ratio (raman_spectra). Asserted: the stretch frequency 1441.64 cm^-1 (rtol 0.01), d alpha_zz / d z_Li = -13.5330 and d alpha_zz / d z_H = +13.4900 (rows 50, 53; rtol 0.02; their sum is the translational-invariance residual, 0.3 %), activity 349.51 A^4/amu (rtol 0.02), depolarization ratio 0.0328 (rtol 0.05). For reading, not asserted: the removed molresponse_v2 engine gave 1427.94 cm^-1, 350.59 A^4/amu, 0.0323 and d alpha_zz/d z_Li = -13.502 at protocol [1e-4, 1e-5], l 80 (archived LiH reference); DALTON HF/aug-cc-pVQZ at this geometry gives 1427.02 cm^-1, 348.84 A^4/amu, 0.03254; this deck at protocol [1e-4, 1e-6], l 80 gives 1430.15 / 350.83 / 0.03254. Response dconv 1e-4 under the relative FD gate (||dx|| <= atol + 5 dconv ||x||): every leg converges in 6-9 iterations (under the earlier absolute gate the ~1e3-norm nuclear legs needed dconv 1e-3, which gave 350.43 A^4/amu and d alpha_zz/d z_Li = -13.5346). Nothing here is a converged Raman value. Under the purification rule the LiH Hessian is built from the Li response states alone (heavier atom's row wins), so the frequency is insensitive to the H legs. Reference: RelWithDebInfo, Pthreads, ArmPL, 1 rank x 10 threads, dd (Neoverse-N1), 2026-10-16, madqc/checkpoint-publication-raman at 2a3d92920 + regenerated references, wall 255 s.",
